==Strategy==
==='''Chapter 1'''===
The threats of the stage are the Hippoe variants. Definitely bring a critter like [[Jurassic Cat (Rare Cat)|Jurassic Cat Sitter]] to hard counter to Metal Hippoe. Bring a unit like [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Artist Cat]] to counter the Gabriels, but may help in defeating Metal Hippoe as well as he has a quick attack rate. For Zomboe, use a good anti-Zombie like [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Sifu Cat]], as he counters Zoge and Zomboe sufficiently. For Hyppoe, use [[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Rover Cat Mk II]] and [[Wheel Cat (Rare Cat)|Solar Cat]]. If struggling with Doge Dark, try to burst him down with high damage attackers like [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|King Dragon Cat]].

==='''Chapter 2'''===
Bring both anti-Zombie and anti-Alien to this stage. The threats of this stage are the magnified Metal Hippoe and Cyberhorn. Make sure to bring critters like [[Jurassic Cat (Rare Cat)|Catasaurus]] to this stage to counter Metal Hippoe. To counter Cyberhorn, use units like [[Psychocat (Rare Cat)|Neo Psychocat]], [[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Rover Cat Mk II]], [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Castaway Cat]], etc.

==='''Chapter 3'''===
It is absolutely essential to use [[Jurassic Cat (Rare Cat)|Catasaurus]] or critters in general for this stage due to the presence of Metal Doge who in which is also accompanied by Metal Hippoe. Use units similar to the previously mentioned [[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Rover Cat Mk II]] and [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Castaway Cat]] to deal with the greatly magnified Cyberhorn and Shibaliens. Bring [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] with the Extra Money ability if you can for a better economy, specifically for Shibalien and Doge Dark.

